# TypeScript rules

- TypeScript strict mode must stay enabled.
- No `any` unless explicitly justified in a comment and review.
- Do not use `@ts-ignore` to hide design/type errors.
- Prefer discriminated unions for domain states/actions.
- Prefer small pure functions for domain/math code.
- React components must not contain poker formulas.
- No duplicated domain constants.
- No floating-point representation for chip amounts; chips are integers.
- Validate data at domain boundaries.
- Errors shown to the user must be understandable Russian text.
- Do not swallow exceptions with empty catch blocks.
- Dependencies require a short justification and should be hidden behind our own adapter when they implement core poker logic.
